WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:02.268
A simple
coil of copper wire.

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.236
One battery.

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.437
One magnet.

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:06.773
This is the world's
simplest motor.

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.842
It will spin
until this battery runs out

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:10.110
quietly, smoothly, while

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.745
generating very little heat.

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:13.780
What's widely misunderstood
is that

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.148
this is why rare

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.649
earth
minerals are so critical.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.985
They are how we create
magnets.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:20.453
Take a hunk of metal.

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:21.354
Melt it down.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.390
Add one of the magnet rare
earth metals to it.

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:25.792
Let it cool and you perform
something close to magic.

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:26.993
You've transformed it into

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.194
a permanent magnet.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:28.895
Irreplaceable.

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:29.996
Because there's nothing on
Earth

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.264
that generates as much force

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:32.899
as magnets, yet waste
so little.

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.300
AirPods have six magnets

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.903
iPhone 14, laptop
at least a dozen.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:38.338
The reason
electric cars work

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:40.473
is because there's 12
pounds of it in the motor.

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:42.142
There are at least 12 rare
earth

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:43.476
magnets in every missile
the U.S.

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:44.344
military uses.

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:45.345
That's how they steer.

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:46.880
So if you wanted
to hurt a country

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.314
to put their businesses
in a bad

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:49.749
spot, hurt their military.

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:51.518
Then these are the rare
earth minerals

00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:53.953
to make sure they can't
get their hands on something

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:56.456
only one country can do,
because one country controls

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.691
94% of all magnet
rare earths.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:00.393
When people say China has

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:01.961
monopoly on rare earths,

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:03.296
this is what they're
talking about

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:05.832
and what the world is
now scrambling to overcome.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:08.701
This video is

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:09.903
sponsored by Zotac.

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.104
More on them later.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:12.439
A magnet already

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:14.040
has a field around it,
an invisible

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.275
bubble of push and pull.

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:17.210
A plain copper
wire does not,

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:19.312
but send electricity
through that wire.

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:20.880
And for as long as
the current is flowing,

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:22.749
the wire grows
a field of its own.

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.551
It becomes a temporary
magnet.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.853
The fancy word for
this is electromagnetism.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.054
Now you have two magnets

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.255
in one tiny arena.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.223
One is permanent.

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:32.358
One only lives while
the battery is connected.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.060
And magnets
that share a space

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.295
do what magnets always do.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:37.030
They try to force the other
to move.

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:38.264
That forced movement

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.499
in a simple setup like this,

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:41.334
where they're held in place
but allowed to spin.

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:42.635
That movement is rotation.

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:44.571
That rotation is a motor
crank.

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:45.939
The current,
the copper wire becomes

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:47.273
a stronger, temporary
magnet.

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.308
Faster. Shove.

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:50.143
Park a second magnet across
from the first,

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:51.478
and the coil becomes trapped

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:52.679
in a tug of war,

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.214
which is pretty fun
to play with

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:55.415
and can change the objective

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:57.817
from spin to point
in a specific direction.

00:01:57.851 --> 00:01:59.519
The entire modern
electric world

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:00.787
is this interaction, shrunk

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.155
and repeated
a thousand times.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:03.723
Electricity creates a field.

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.391
The field fights
a real magnet.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:06.993
Something useful moves.

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:08.628
They were heavy,

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.530
not particularly strong,
had problems

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.398
with high temperatures,
but got the job done.

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:14.400
When we first figured out
how to make magnets.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.802
Virtually
every magnet was made out

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:17.003
of iron or aluminum.

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:19.305
This type of magnet actually
helped win World War Two.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:21.174
They were the foundation
of the radar system

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:23.576
that allowed Allied planes
to see German U-boats.

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:25.278
So fittingly,
it was two Air Force

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:27.413
engineers who put cobalt
and samarium together.

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:28.882
25 years after the war,

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:30.717
the world's first rare
earth magnet was born.

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:32.986
It was lighter, stronger
and critically handled

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.621
extreme temperatures
very well, but

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:35.989
it started out expensive

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:37.223
and then got more expensive

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.626
as the Congo
fell into a huge civil war.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:42.362
This is the place where
95% of cobalt came from.

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:45.431
Still, the majority of it
comes from their prices rose

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:46.699
and they rose a lot, up

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:48.234
400% in less than a year.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.636
So again, quite naturally,

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:51.738
trying to escape these
high prices, wanting

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:52.972
more magnets, desperately

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:54.340
wanting them to be cheaper.

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:56.910
Five years later,
two companies who really saw

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.378
the promise of magnets
in everyday

00:02:58.378 --> 00:03:00.280
life, General Motors
and the company

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.714
that would become Hitachi
Metals,

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:03.016
get on stage at a conference

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:04.417
and reveal the neodymium

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:05.618
iron boron magnet.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:06.352
Now, this part

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:07.754
of General Motors
that invented

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:08.755
a version of these magnets.

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.657
As you'll see shortly,
this is not the end of

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:11.224
their story.

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:13.259
They will go on
to become central in that.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.294
How did China manage

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:15.695
to build a monopoly
around this stuff?

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:16.262
Question.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.464
Anyway, these new magnets
were smaller,

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:19.832
much cheaper, three times

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:21.034
cheaper, more powerful.

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:23.236
This was the magnet
that would change the world.

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:24.504
GM used it immediately to

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:26.973
cut the size of the starter
motor in all of its cars

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:28.341
in half everything

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:30.443
that would have been better
with a magnet or impossible

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:31.978
without one started
getting one.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:34.080
Power windows, power locks,
windshield wipers,

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.515
cordless tools
that didn't feel like boat

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:37.717
anchors, hard drives
that could finally fit

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:39.219
serious storage
into a laptop,

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.954
your phone, speakers,
refrigerators,

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:42.455
the motors
that make electric cars

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:44.224
a reality
instead of theoretical.

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:46.059
Try to escape
rare earth magnets and you

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.393
pay for it in size, weight,

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.695
efficiency, or price.

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:49.829
It's not a nice to have.

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:51.331
This is the material
that let us

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:52.865
shrink the electric world.

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:54.400
That is why for every dollar

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.935
that flows through the rare
earth industry,

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:58.037
$0.96 of it
ends up in magnets,

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.772
almost all of it
flowing into China,

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:01.107
a country that was making

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:02.675
exactly zero magnets back

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:05.511
when the neodymium magnet
was invented in 1983.

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:06.813
Did China do this
intentionally?

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:08.147
They did move by move,

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:10.383
pulling the entire industry
into their control.

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:11.618
But how they managed to

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:13.353
do this over
the course of two decades

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:16.189
is only one half
of a very interesting story.

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:17.390
The other half?

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:18.791
Did you know rare

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:20.426
earths aren't actually rare?

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.428
China
did not build its monopoly

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.631
because it's the only one
that has these rare earths.

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:25.898
China built its monopoly

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:28.268
by doing the thing
no one else wanted to.

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:30.403
Separating them
from the dirt and rocks

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:31.571
there founded.

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:32.772
Every circle on

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:34.073
this map is a rare earth
deposit,

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:35.575
a place
where we know that mixing

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:36.943
with the dirt
and rocks in the ground.

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:38.778
There are also
a bunch of rare earths.

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:40.179
The bigger the circle,
the more rare

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:42.115
earths would come up
with each scoop of Earth,

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:43.616
you have a surplus of
what are called light

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:44.851
rare earths neodymium.

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.620
In many places,
the heavier rare earths,

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.055
the process samarium,

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:50.890
the ones the US
military is interested in,

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.625
those are a bit harder
to find.

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:55.361
Looking at this, we can see
that when people say

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:57.530
where earths aren't rare,
they're telling the truth.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.732
And this is perhaps
the most famous

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.901
of all the rare earth mines
mountain pass

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.303
found
in Southern California,

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:04.971
