It takes 3 to 5 years.

00:16:53.912 --> 00:16:55.681
China can set a watch by it.

00:16:55.681 --> 00:16:56.982
By the time those years

00:16:56.982 --> 00:16:58.550
pass, much has changed.

00:16:58.584 --> 00:17:00.586
A lot of foreign competitors
are bleeding by the end,

00:17:00.619 --> 00:17:01.820
smothered by high prices

00:17:01.820 --> 00:17:03.455
and new cheap competition.

00:17:03.455 --> 00:17:05.557
Meanwhile, Chinese plants
have absorbed

00:17:05.557 --> 00:17:07.626
a huge amount of skills,
know how and data.

00:17:07.626 --> 00:17:09.862
But the high prices also did
something

00:17:09.895 --> 00:17:11.597
China does not want long
term.

00:17:11.597 --> 00:17:13.265
They tempted new mines
and refiners

00:17:13.265 --> 00:17:15.401
to open in Canada,
Australia, the US.

00:17:15.467 --> 00:17:17.503
So when the door swings
wide open

00:17:17.503 --> 00:17:18.937
supply pours onto the world.

00:17:18.937 --> 00:17:21.573
That price is so low
the new guys can't dig rock

00:17:21.573 --> 00:17:23.742
for less than China's
selling finished material.

00:17:23.776 --> 00:17:24.977
Company after company

00:17:24.977 --> 00:17:26.378
goes under inside

00:17:26.378 --> 00:17:27.813
China,
what started as dozens

00:17:27.813 --> 00:17:29.481
or hundreds of companies,
they all get

00:17:29.481 --> 00:17:30.749
folded and merged
into a couple

00:17:30.783 --> 00:17:32.051
of giant state run

00:17:32.051 --> 00:17:33.619
champions for rare earths.

00:17:33.619 --> 00:17:34.820
That's China Northern Rare
Earth

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:36.355
Group and China
Rare Earth Group.

00:17:36.355 --> 00:17:38.457
So China ends up
with two giant state

00:17:38.457 --> 00:17:40.025
champions on rare earths,

00:17:40.426 --> 00:17:41.860
which sounds like
the end of the story.

00:17:41.860 --> 00:17:42.861
It is not.

00:17:42.861 --> 00:17:44.663
We are at the part
where the story

00:17:44.663 --> 00:17:47.099
gets smaller and stranger,
because the piece of this

00:17:47.099 --> 00:17:48.667
monopoly
that actually keeps people

00:17:48.667 --> 00:17:49.935
in the military up at night

00:17:49.935 --> 00:17:51.270
is not rare earths.

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:53.772
As a category, it is a
thin slice of the category,

00:17:53.839 --> 00:17:55.340
a metal that does not
show up in the big,

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:56.675
shiny rare earth headline,
the way

00:17:56.708 --> 00:17:57.910
neodymium does

00:17:57.943 --> 00:18:00.279
a metal tied to a particular
kind of dirty

00:18:00.312 --> 00:18:01.480
ground in southern China.

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:02.915
Sticky red clay country,

00:18:02.948 --> 00:18:04.483
a much different thing
from digging

00:18:04.483 --> 00:18:06.118
or out of the ground
in the north.

00:18:06.118 --> 00:18:07.352
Before
I give you the name, now

00:18:07.519 --> 00:18:09.021
picture the job
it has to do.

00:18:09.054 --> 00:18:11.390
A cruise missile
leaves a ship, it drops low.

00:18:11.390 --> 00:18:12.791
It flies
for hundreds of miles,

00:18:12.791 --> 00:18:14.993
maybe thousands of miles,
reading the terrain,

00:18:14.993 --> 00:18:16.562
twitching
its fins a degree at a time

00:18:16.562 --> 00:18:17.896
so it can put itself
through a window

00:18:17.896 --> 00:18:20.199
or into a bunker
without a pilot on board.

00:18:20.265 --> 00:18:22.101
Those little twitches
are magnets, fighting

00:18:22.101 --> 00:18:23.502
electricity and a tiny motor

00:18:23.502 --> 00:18:24.736
at the base of each fin.

00:18:24.736 --> 00:18:26.672
And those magnets
only keep their strength

00:18:26.672 --> 00:18:28.340
in these real world
conditions.

00:18:28.373 --> 00:18:29.141
Heat, stress.

00:18:29.141 --> 00:18:32.077
Time if the recipe used to
make them includes this one

00:18:32.111 --> 00:18:33.745
hard to get ingredient

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:35.814
overnight.

00:18:35.814 --> 00:18:38.717
And for the second day,
the American ship

00:18:38.717 --> 00:18:40.819
launched their Tomahawk
cruise missiles.

00:18:40.819 --> 00:18:43.188
100 of these were fired
in the first 24 hours

00:18:43.188 --> 00:18:44.656
of the Gulf
War, striking command

00:18:44.723 --> 00:18:46.658
centers, air
defenses, and power stations

00:18:46.658 --> 00:18:47.693
all across Iraq

00:18:47.693 --> 00:18:49.461
well before any soldiers
were on the ground,

00:18:49.495 --> 00:18:51.497
hitting the most heavily
defended targets in Iraq

00:18:51.497 --> 00:18:53.732
without risking anyone
that night is the reason

00:18:53.732 --> 00:18:54.933
the Tomahawk became
the missile

00:18:54.933 --> 00:18:55.734
you see on the news.

00:18:55.734 --> 00:18:58.237
Most information
about them is classified,

00:18:58.237 --> 00:18:59.471
but we know for sure

00:18:59.471 --> 00:19:01.106
that to steer itself
to the target,

00:19:01.106 --> 00:19:02.975
each one needs
at least 12 magnets.

00:19:03.041 --> 00:19:04.543
You will find them right
at the base of each

00:19:04.576 --> 00:19:06.612
fin, positioned inside
a coil of copper.

00:19:06.612 --> 00:19:08.147
Anytime
the computer on board says

00:19:08.147 --> 00:19:10.215
we need to adjust course,
electricity flows

00:19:10.215 --> 00:19:11.717
into the wire,
around the magnets,

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:12.985
the rod they're connected to

00:19:13.018 --> 00:19:14.987
turns
and then holds its position.

00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:17.055
The rod isn't mechanically
locked into place.

00:19:17.055 --> 00:19:18.357
It's kept in that position

00:19:18.357 --> 00:19:19.558
by keeping electricity

00:19:19.558 --> 00:19:21.026
flowing through the wire.

00:19:23.162 --> 00:19:24.096
Energy can't be

00:19:24.096 --> 00:19:25.597
created
and it can't be destroyed.

00:19:25.597 --> 00:19:27.533
It can only be converted
or transferred.

00:19:27.533 --> 00:19:30.102
This according to the first
law of thermodynamics.

00:19:30.102 --> 00:19:32.471
So the electricity
flowing in to hold that fin

00:19:32.471 --> 00:19:34.973
in its new position, since
it isn't moving anything,

00:19:35.073 --> 00:19:36.909
it generates
heat, a lot of it.

00:19:36.909 --> 00:19:38.277
And if there's one thing
that magnets

00:19:38.277 --> 00:19:39.711
don't like, it is heat.

00:19:39.745 --> 00:19:42.414
As a magnet gets hotter,
it loses power, get too hot,

00:19:42.414 --> 00:19:44.950
and it can permanently
destroy the magnetic pole.

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.552
So just like this motor,

00:19:46.552 --> 00:19:47.753
we can get the same effect

00:19:47.753 --> 00:19:49.922
with less powerful
but heavier magnets.

00:19:49.922 --> 00:19:51.456
These are ceramic magnets.

00:19:51.456 --> 00:19:53.258
They have no rare
earths in them,

00:19:53.258 --> 00:19:54.493
so for three times

00:19:54.493 --> 00:19:55.861
the weight and three times

00:19:55.861 --> 00:19:57.062
the size, we get

00:19:57.062 --> 00:19:58.330
the same amount of power

00:19:58.330 --> 00:20:00.065
as these neodymium magnets.

00:20:04.136 --> 00:20:04.536
You could

00:20:04.536 --> 00:20:05.737
fight heat the same way.

00:20:05.737 --> 00:20:06.071
Okay.

00:20:06.071 --> 00:20:07.506
Loses about 50% power

00:20:07.506 --> 00:20:08.740
after flying for an hour.

00:20:08.774 --> 00:20:10.475
We'll just double the size
of the magnet.

00:20:10.475 --> 00:20:11.910
But in something
so intricate

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:13.912
as a Tomahawk missile,
where would you put it?

00:20:13.912 --> 00:20:15.113
And even if you did

00:20:15.113 --> 00:20:16.982
decide to do that,
you'd have to do all sorts

00:20:16.982 --> 00:20:18.617
of new testing
certification.

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:19.985
The process alone would be

00:20:19.985 --> 00:20:21.186
a major hassle

00:20:21.186 --> 00:20:22.754
to end up
with a worse missile.

00:20:22.754 --> 00:20:24.556
And this is just
one type of missile

00:20:24.556 --> 00:20:26.024
the US military uses.

00:20:26.058 --> 00:20:28.227
It would be better instead
if there was some magic

00:20:28.227 --> 00:20:30.395
ingredient that made them
heat resistant.

00:20:30.395 --> 00:20:32.197
Something like samarium.

00:20:32.231 --> 00:20:34.600
Sure enough, that's
what the US military uses

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:35.801
for magnets, cutting

00:20:35.801 --> 00:20:38.070
that temperature problem
by 95%.

00:20:38.103 --> 00:20:39.771
And sure enough,
that is the rare earth

00:20:39.771 --> 00:20:41.607
China has not a 94%
monopoly on,

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:44.142
but a 99% monopoly
on taking about a third

00:20:44.142 --> 00:20:45.510
more steps, costing 12 times

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:46.945
more to refine
than neodymium,

00:20:46.945 --> 00:20:48.714
and found in fewer places
in the ground.

00:20:48.714 --> 00:20:50.015
When China fully banned

00:20:50.082 --> 00:20:51.516
exports of samarium
in response

00:20:51.516 --> 00:20:52.317
to tariffs being put up,

00:20:52.317 --> 00:20:54.019
they knew exactly how it was
being used.

00:20:54.019 --> 00:20:55.520
And I quote this reflects

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:56.788
China's consistent stance

00:20:56.788 --> 00:20:57.990
on upholding world peace

00:20:57.990 --> 00:20:59.258
and regional stability.

00:20:59.491 --> 00:21:00.459
You would not ban this stuff

00:21:00.459 --> 00:21:02.461
and then mention peace
if it was a military thing

00:21:02.494 --> 00:21:05.063
to which a lot of people
around the world answered,

00:21:05.097 --> 00:21:06.732
this is unacceptable.

00:21:06.732 --> 00:21:08.900
I think it's time
for a Manhattan Project

00:21:08.900 --> 00:21:10.636
like effort to end our rare

00:21:10.669 --> 00:21:12.271
earth dependency on China.

00:21:12.304 --> 00:21:14.039
Yet the United States
remains dangerously

00:21:14.039 --> 00:21:15.274
dependent
on foreign countries,

00:21:15.274 --> 00:21:17.175
including China,
for this critical mineral.

00:21:17.175 --> 00:21:18.810
This is not a
theoretical risk.

00:21:18.810 --> 00:21:20.012
It is a clear and present

00:21:20.012 --> 00:21:21.546
danger
to our national security.

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:23.682
The thing is, a lot of
people knew this already.

00:21:23.715 --> 00:21:25.550
It just wasn't your mom
or the bartender

00:21:25.584 --> 00:21:26.985
guy from work
that you grab a beer with.

00:21:26.985 --> 00:21:28.620
Sometimes
for at least two decades

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:30.956
in the halls of the Pentagon
subcommittees in Congress,

00:21:30.956 --> 00:21:32.691
people would say,
this is a problem.

00:21:32.691 --> 00:21:33.492
China is doing this

00:21:33.492 --> 00:21:35.060
so they can cut us off
in the future.

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:36.495
It's not that people thought

00:21:36.495 --> 00:21:38.196
the people making
these claims were wrong

00:21:38.196 --> 00:21:39.665
or didn't know what
they were talking about.

00:21:39.665 --> 00:21:41.433
It just wasn't clear that
China ever would.

00:21:41.466 --> 00:21:42.200
So for years,

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:43.468
it could only ever hang

00:21:43.502 --> 00:21:45.070
around as one of those
suspicions of

00:21:45.103 --> 00:21:46.505
what if that could happen?

00:21:46.538 --> 00:21:47.739
Like that one friend,

00:21:48.140 --> 00:21:49.174
we have way less oil

00:21:49.174 --> 00:21:50.842
than they tell us this year.

00:21:50.876 --> 00:21:52.477
Maybe two three at tops.

00:21:52.477 --> 00:21:53.478
The wells are going dry.

00:21:53.478 --> 00:21:55.714
It's going
full mad Max the story

00:21:55.714 --> 00:21:57.215
and said it really wasn't
even a story.

00:21:57.215 --> 00:21:59.117
It was just an observation
of what appeared

00:21:59.117 --> 00:22:00.352
to be the game on the field.

00:22:00.385 --> 00:22:01.586
China got the pollution
and the

00:22:01.586 --> 00:22:03.755
