paying $200 for Ray-Bans.

00:23:16.595 --> 00:23:17.863
That cost $7 to make

00:23:17.863 --> 00:23:20.699
for two reasons one,
using it to force people

00:23:20.699 --> 00:23:23.468
to act in a certain way that
makes people feel trapped.

00:23:23.468 --> 00:23:25.170
Crossing
the line makes the customer

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:27.339
feel like they were kidnaped
and is now a hostage,

00:23:27.372 --> 00:23:28.340
especially if it's something

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:29.641
required
for the world to work.

00:23:29.674 --> 00:23:30.776
It just doesn't sit well.

00:23:30.776 --> 00:23:32.310
You get this
kind of reaction.

00:23:32.344 --> 00:23:33.912
China's sweeping
export controls

00:23:33.912 --> 00:23:36.415
this year were a significant
wake up call.

00:23:36.415 --> 00:23:38.417
They disrupted supply
chains, triggered

00:23:38.417 --> 00:23:40.318
factory shutdowns
in the United States.

00:23:40.318 --> 00:23:42.454
It wasn't
just a handful of years ago

00:23:42.521 --> 00:23:44.856
that policymakers recognized

00:23:44.856 --> 00:23:46.057
that we have a problem,

00:23:46.091 --> 00:23:48.026
our dependency on China

00:23:48.193 --> 00:23:50.962
for critical minerals,
for more importantly,

00:23:50.962 --> 00:23:51.696
number two,

00:23:51.696 --> 00:23:53.899
the people who said
it was a deliberate strategy

00:23:53.899 --> 00:23:55.400
to exert
control in the world are now

00:23:55.400 --> 00:23:56.234
proven correct.

00:23:56.234 --> 00:23:57.469
The people who didn't
listen to them

00:23:57.469 --> 00:23:58.837
before
start listening intently.

00:23:58.837 --> 00:23:59.438
And the happy

00:23:59.438 --> 00:24:01.339
story of a clean trade
between two countries.

00:24:01.339 --> 00:24:03.508
It evaporates, the retelling
of which is replaced

00:24:03.508 --> 00:24:05.944
by cold analysis
of every other situation

00:24:05.944 --> 00:24:07.379
where the pattern showed up

00:24:07.412 --> 00:24:08.814
solar, cars, aluminum.

00:24:08.814 --> 00:24:09.514
Every motive

00:24:09.514 --> 00:24:11.149
that was assumed
is now questioned,

00:24:11.149 --> 00:24:13.452
even if it came
from being provoked.

00:24:13.518 --> 00:24:14.953
The US started cutting China

00:24:14.953 --> 00:24:16.388
off from the best
semiconductors

00:24:16.555 --> 00:24:17.756
at about 2016

00:24:17.756 --> 00:24:19.658
and really clamped down
in 2019,

00:24:19.691 --> 00:24:22.828
upped it again in 2020 and
then big tariffs in 2025.

00:24:22.861 --> 00:24:24.896
So yes, the US
did provoke China

00:24:24.896 --> 00:24:26.531
with this stuff,
no question about that.

00:24:26.531 --> 00:24:27.933
But the whole period
of the US

00:24:27.933 --> 00:24:29.835
chips industry
before this started,

00:24:29.835 --> 00:24:32.103
the right word
would be organic.

00:24:32.137 --> 00:24:34.072
Hundreds of firms competing,
the government

00:24:34.105 --> 00:24:36.508
not intervening to prevent
foreign firms from winning.

00:24:36.541 --> 00:24:39.144
No government
backstop Intel was crushed.

00:24:39.144 --> 00:24:40.612
Over the last two decades
in the US,

00:24:40.612 --> 00:24:42.948
chip industry
as a whole was hollowed out

00:24:42.948 --> 00:24:45.417
by Japan and Taiwan
in the 90s and 2000.

00:24:45.450 --> 00:24:47.118
The US government
didn't intervene.

00:24:47.118 --> 00:24:48.920
It didn't
build it up on purpose,

00:24:48.920 --> 00:24:50.422
so then it could take it
away.

00:24:50.455 --> 00:24:52.157
That is why,
to many observers,

00:24:52.157 --> 00:24:54.659
the rare earth situation
from China feels different,

00:24:54.659 --> 00:24:56.228
that it feels like
this whole time

00:24:56.228 --> 00:24:58.230
the Chinese government
was executing a plan

00:24:58.230 --> 00:24:59.498
drawn up on a whiteboard

00:24:59.498 --> 00:25:00.866
to control
a critical industry

00:25:00.866 --> 00:25:01.800
so that once under

00:25:01.800 --> 00:25:03.535
their control,
they could take it away

00:25:03.535 --> 00:25:06.338
if they wanted to, that it
was definitely not organic.

00:25:06.338 --> 00:25:08.974
It was planned control
of all the trade moves

00:25:08.974 --> 00:25:11.243
between the US and China
over the past decade.

00:25:11.276 --> 00:25:13.378
The rare earths
one was the most extreme

00:25:13.378 --> 00:25:15.080
because publicly revealing

00:25:15.080 --> 00:25:17.883
your monopoly has zero long
term upside.

00:25:17.883 --> 00:25:19.184
It's usually reserved for

00:25:19.184 --> 00:25:20.385
when war is breaking out,

00:25:20.385 --> 00:25:21.987
because you want to play
the card

00:25:21.987 --> 00:25:23.355
as a last resort only

00:25:23.355 --> 00:25:24.556
when it really matters.

00:25:24.589 --> 00:25:26.157
Otherwise,
you will encourage

00:25:26.157 --> 00:25:27.359
everyone to immediately
start

00:25:27.359 --> 00:25:29.861
solving the problem,
which is exactly what

00:25:29.861 --> 00:25:31.196
the world is doing
right now.

00:25:31.263 --> 00:25:33.798
Japan, Australia,
and particularly the US

00:25:33.798 --> 00:25:36.234
have made the moves required
to break the monopoly.

00:25:36.268 --> 00:25:38.637
The Pentagon has made deals
with companies guaranteeing

00:25:38.637 --> 00:25:40.338
they'll pay $110 per

00:25:40.338 --> 00:25:42.841
kilogram of rare earths,
well above the market price.

00:25:42.841 --> 00:25:44.709
That way,
China can't flood the market

00:25:44.709 --> 00:25:46.511
and wash out US
companies again.

00:25:46.545 --> 00:25:48.547
Things like this have
happened in the US before.

00:25:48.580 --> 00:25:49.981
The aluminum industry
around World

00:25:49.981 --> 00:25:51.283
War two being one,

00:25:51.316 --> 00:25:53.251
the US needed a lot
of aluminum for planes.

00:25:53.251 --> 00:25:54.920
This was
the start of the plane era

00:25:54.920 --> 00:25:56.588
and that capacity
just wasn't there yet.

00:25:56.588 --> 00:25:58.156
But this one for rare
earths, it's

00:25:58.156 --> 00:25:58.857
a little different.

00:25:58.857 --> 00:26:00.659
Not only are they
guaranteeing the price,

00:26:00.659 --> 00:26:02.227
they're also guaranteeing
an amount.

00:26:02.227 --> 00:26:04.195
They'll buy an arrangement
called take or pay.

00:26:04.195 --> 00:26:06.431
But if the market
price is over $110,

00:26:06.431 --> 00:26:07.732
the government gets 30%

00:26:07.732 --> 00:26:10.068
of the difference between
100 and $10 and the higher

00:26:10.068 --> 00:26:11.536
price for whatever else

00:26:11.536 --> 00:26:12.837
they sell to whoever else.

00:26:12.837 --> 00:26:14.239
So there's upside
in this deal

00:26:14.239 --> 00:26:15.774
that is guaranteed
for ten years.

00:26:15.774 --> 00:26:17.342
This is all happening
largely.

00:26:17.342 --> 00:26:18.777
And of course it is
by extending

00:26:18.777 --> 00:26:20.912
the saga of Mountain Pass,
which is what this deal is

00:26:20.912 --> 00:26:22.681
aimed
at, the miners back online,

00:26:22.681 --> 00:26:23.348
not only mining,

00:26:23.348 --> 00:26:24.783
but now
processing and refining

00:26:24.783 --> 00:26:26.151
rare earths
and building an advanced

00:26:26.151 --> 00:26:27.819
processing facility
in Texas.

00:26:27.852 --> 00:26:29.020
These are the moves
that you would need

00:26:29.020 --> 00:26:30.589
to make to get the industry
rolling again.

00:26:30.622 --> 00:26:31.456
Will it work?

00:26:31.456 --> 00:26:32.057
We'll see.

00:26:32.057 --> 00:26:33.391
It's an uncommon arrangement

00:26:33.391 --> 00:26:35.594
in the US,
but it's not unprecedented.

